/T (The report explains the measurements carried out by Group 07 on five datasets \(GOOSE, MAN TruckScenes, TruckDrive, STONE and RADIATE\) and what each of the results does and does not show. It is based on the project's twenty evidence-linked findings, which are set out below in the form of five main messages. Each of the numbers can be traced back to a saved result record, an experiment log or an evidence file in the project repository. )
/E (The report explains the measurements carried out by Group 07 on five datasets \(GOOSE, MAN TruckScenes, TruckDrive, STONE and RADIATE\) and what each of the results does and does not show. It is based on the project's twenty evidence-linked findings, which are set out below in the form of five main messages. Each of the numbers can be traced back to a saved result record, an experiment log or an evidence file in the project repository. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 226 0 R
/T (The headline states that, in TruckDrive with the only dataset we have containing labelled vehicles at a distance of 200 to 400 metres, LiDAR returns were more often found inside the labelled vehicles than radar returns were. We were unable to use this to carry out a detection comparison since no available pretrained model takes input at that range. Consequently, the project's initial hypothesis, that 4D radar would degrade less than LiDAR at long range, is not supported by our geometric evidence and has not yet been tested as a detection issue. )
/E (The headline states that, in TruckDrive with the only dataset we have containing labelled vehicles at a distance of 200 to 400 metres, LiDAR returns were more often found inside the labelled vehicles than radar returns were. We were unable to use this to carry out a detection comparison since no available pretrained model takes input at that range. Consequently, the project's initial hypothesis, that 4D radar would degrade less than LiDAR at long range, is not supported by our geometric evidence and has not yet been tested as a detection issue. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
