/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (The aim of the project is to carry out an evidence-based comparison of the ways in which RADAR, LiDAR and camera systems perceive their environment in the context of autonomous trucking, by using existing open-source models on public datasets which have been recorded in a reproducible manner and then provided as a fully documented body of work. The main research question \(D-04\) is whether the current models fail beyond a distance of about 150 metres and whether 4D radar degrades less than LiDAR at that range. Each of the datasets was used as a tool for addressing a different aspect of that question. )
/E (The aim of the project is to carry out an evidence-based comparison of the ways in which RADAR, LiDAR and camera systems perceive their environment in the context of autonomous trucking, by using existing open-source models on public datasets which have been recorded in a reproducible manner and then provided as a fully documented body of work. The main research question \(D-04\) is whether the current models fail beyond a distance of about 150 metres and whether 4D radar degrades less than LiDAR at that range. Each of the datasets was used as a tool for addressing a different aspect of that question. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
