/T (4. A ground label by itself is not sufficient to indicate the space available for a vehicle; within a distance of 25 metres, 43.46% of the half-metre map cells showed no return, obstacle returns were at varying heights, and in order to require support over a 2.5 m square only 23.48% of the positions which had passed a single-cell check were retained. These diagnostics show which information should be preserved for navigation; they do not prove that a clearance or a route exists \(Section 3.4\). )
/E (4. A ground label by itself is not sufficient to indicate the space available for a vehicle; within a distance of 25 metres, 43.46% of the half-metre map cells showed no return, obstacle returns were at varying heights, and in order to require support over a 2.5 m square only 23.48% of the positions which had passed a single-cell check were retained. These diagnostics show which information should be preserved for navigation; they do not prove that a clearance or a route exists \(Section 3.4\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (5. Any future improvements to the model must include tests which are capable of revealing regressions and reflect the way the model is intended to be used. With more model context, six out of the seven held-out terrain frames were improved, one was made worse, and processing time increased by about 28%. A combined soil score of 99.53% masked a rainy-recording result of 7.92%. Water has not yet been tested \(as stated in Sections 3.3 and 3.5\). )
/E (5. Any future improvements to the model must include tests which are capable of revealing regressions and reflect the way the model is intended to be used. With more model context, six out of the seven held-out terrain frames were improved, one was made worse, and processing time increased by about 28%. A combined soil score of 99.53% masked a rainy-recording result of 7.92%. Water has not yet been tested \(as stated in Sections 3.3 and 3.5\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
