645 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 240 0 R
/T (This is the principal long-range outcome of the project. At 200-400m, in 504 vehicle observations LiDAR achieved at least one return within 80.36% of labelled vehicle boxes and radar within 37.50% \(static calibration\). LiDAR dominates at 200m+ in all four eligible scenes under both timing assumptions; below 150m the difference becomes small and occasionally reversed. Equal weighting of scenes gives LiDAR a 38.17% point advantage \(static\) and 44.09% \(aligned\), and removing any single scene leaves LiDAR with at least 31.85 and 37.75%. )
/E (This is the principal long-range outcome of the project. At 200-400m, in 504 vehicle observations LiDAR achieved at least one return within 80.36% of labelled vehicle boxes and radar within 37.50% \(static calibration\). LiDAR dominates at 200m+ in all four eligible scenes under both timing assumptions; below 150m the difference becomes small and occasionally reversed. Equal weighting of scenes gives LiDAR a 38.17% point advantage \(static\) and 44.09% \(aligned\), and removing any single scene leaves LiDAR with at least 31.85 and 37.75%. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
646 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 240 0 R
/T (Hold-out check. Two clips \(28_3 and 28_15\) not previously used were sampled at timestamps chosen before any sensor scoring. At 200-400m there are 36 vehicle observations on 18 tracks. LiDAR achieved 86.11% support and radar 33.33% under alignment hypothesis \(static: 80.56% and 36.11%\), LiDAR ahead in both clips. A single radar-only observation raised support from either sensor to 88.89%, showing that radar sometimes provides evidence not available to LiDAR. )
/E (Hold-out check. Two clips \(28_3 and 28_15\) not previously used were sampled at timestamps chosen before any sensor scoring. At 200-400m there are 36 vehicle observations on 18 tracks. LiDAR achieved 86.11% support and radar 33.33% under alignment hypothesis \(static: 80.56% and 36.11%\), LiDAR ahead in both clips. A single radar-only observation raised support from either sensor to 88.89%, showing that radar sometimes provides evidence not available to LiDAR. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
