833 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 246 0 R
/T (Each dataset answers a different question. TruckDrive is the only one that can test long range, and there LiDAR keeps more geometric evidence on distant vehicles than radar. TruckScenes has the best matched sensor suite, but its recorded radar stops near 190 m, and its density control shows how much of a support gap can come from point count alone. GOOSE and STONE cover off-road terrain, where radar sees little ground and a terrain model makes errors in both directions. RADIATE shows radar responding in fog where LiDAR has nothing, though not specifically to vehicles. )
/E (Each dataset answers a different question. TruckDrive is the only one that can test long range, and there LiDAR keeps more geometric evidence on distant vehicles than radar. TruckScenes has the best matched sensor suite, but its recorded radar stops near 190 m, and its density control shows how much of a support gap can come from point count alone. GOOSE and STONE cover off-road terrain, where radar sees little ground and a terrain model makes errors in both directions. RADIATE shows radar responding in fog where LiDAR has nothing, though not specifically to vehicles. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [38]
>>
endobj
