1927 0 obj
<<
/Title (4. A ground label by itself is not sufficient to indicate the space available for a vehicle; within a distance of 25 metres, 43.46% of the half-metre map cells showed no return, obstacle returns were at varying heights, and in order to require support over a 2.5 m square only 23.48% of the positions which had passed a single-cell check were retained. These diagnostics show which information should be preserved for navigation; they do not prove that a clearance or a route exists \(Section 3.4\).)
