3056 0 obj
<<
/Title (This is the principal long-range outcome of the project. At 200-400m, in 504 vehicle observations LiDAR achieved at least one return within 80.36% of labelled vehicle boxes and radar within 37.50% \(static calibration\). LiDAR dominates at 200m+ in all four eligible scenes under both timing assumptions; below 150m the difference becomes small and occasionally reversed. Equal weighting of scenes gives LiDAR a 38.17% point advantage \(static\) and 44.09% \(aligned\), and removing any single scene leaves LiDAR with at least 31.85 and 37.75%.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2872 0 R
/Prev 3032 0 R
/Next 3057 0 R
>>
endobj
3057 0 obj
<<
/Title (Hold-out check. Two clips \(28_3 and 28_15\) not previously used were sampled at timestamps chosen before any sensor scoring. At 200-400m there are 36 vehicle observations on 18 tracks. LiDAR achieved 86.11% support and radar 33.33% under alignment hypothesis \(static: 80.56% and 36.11%\), LiDAR ahead in both clips. A single radar-only observation raised support from either sensor to 88.89%, showing that radar sometimes provides evidence not available to LiDAR.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2872 0 R
/Prev 3056 0 R
/First 3076 0 R
/Last 3076 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 3033 0 R
>>
endobj
